    "narrative": "LawDog\u2019s strongest play for today is **Lawrence Butler**, who leads the rotation with a 74.61 score against Dobnak. The matchup provides a perfect storm of a high-xERA pitcher and a favorable platoon advantage, allowing **Lawrence Butler** to capitalize on the weak opposition. Similarly, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (70.36) remains a set-and-forget anchor; despite a minor platoon penalty, his elite skill set against Roupp makes him a high-floor producer. We are also leaning into **Jonathan Aranda** (67.95) and **Daulton Varsho** (65.74) today, as both leverage significant SP-skill advantages. **Daulton Varsho** specifically benefits from a strong lineup projection, helping him overcome a negative park factor to remain a high-conviction start.\n\nThe decision to start **Zack Gelof** (61.37) over other options was validated by the favorable matchup against Dobnak, though we are closely monitoring the lineup status of **Yainer Diaz** and **Dylan Beavers**. Both carry the \"Lineup Pending\" flag, and while **Dylan Beavers** (55.70) looks promising due to a strong park factor, his output is tempered by the presence of the formidable Gerrit Cole on the mound. Our most difficult bench decision involved weighing the depth of the outfield; **JJ Bleday** (53.26) and **Braden Montgomery** (52.92) were considered, but ultimately, the raw scoring potential of the starters won out. We continue to hold **Bryce Harper**, **Cal Raleigh**, **Justin Crawford**, and **Tyler Freeman** on the bench due to either schedule gaps or active IL status. We remain focused on maximizing volume, though we remain cautious of the potential regression for **Jung Hoo Lee** (44.85), whose matchup against the elite arm of Williams, G leaves little margin for error.",
